. `run` itself could already use that info to fetch file content. We would merge that usually needed step under the control of run, and would have more confidence that we know what the inputs are.\n\nIt doesn't have to super tailored. Even saying `--inputs .` to communicate that I *want* all content to be present for execution would be helpful. A `rerun` could later on make sure that file that were present back then are available now (not necessarily all files that are present in the current state of the repo.)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1524206850,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4Mjk5NzUzNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2291#issuecomment-382997535"},"message":"This is done, but see #2432","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1524206850,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTU4NTQ2MTQwNw=="},"status":2}]}